{"id": "kbc-ghsa-6cr4-ccf3-x7h4", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/sooperset/mcp-atlassian", "sha": "4067d1db4097755cc6add87f95fe3f0746c98c0b", "locator": {"file": "src/mcp_atlassian/confluence/attachments.py", "line": 154, "sink_class": "path-traversal", "symbol": "AttachmentsMixin.upload_attachment"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "confluence_upload_attachment resolved the caller-supplied file_path with os.path.abspath() and opened it with no workspace confinement, so a prompt-injected or authenticated client reads any server file (e.g. /proc/self/environ) and exfiltrates it as a Confluence attachment.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6cr4-ccf3-x7h4", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "b041733473f95119dd539542a43c280737a8e460", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6cr4-ccf3-x7h4", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-6cr4-ccf3-x7h4", "GHSA-p6hp-93wp-fh6p", "GHSA-g5r6-gv6m-f5jv", "GHSA-93xw-j965-9mx3", "GHSA-wm45-qh3g-v83f", "CVE-2026-77259"], "rd_class": "path-traversal", "attacker": "untrusted-llm-input", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Five advisories (same sink, one fix commit). GHSA-6cr4 and GHSA-p6hp are 'incomplete fix of GHSA-xjgw-4wvw-rgm4' (the download-side write was fixed in 0.17.0, the upload-side read was not). Fix is the 0.22.0 omnibus commit."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-f4p7-qx46-wc5j", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/sooperset/mcp-atlassian", "sha": "4067d1db4097755cc6add87f95fe3f0746c98c0b", "locator": {"file": "src/mcp_atlassian/jira/attachments.py", "line": 374, "sink_class": "path-traversal", "symbol": "AttachmentsMixin.upload_attachment"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The Jira upload_attachment tool reads a caller-supplied file_path from the MCP server's filesystem (abspath only, no confinement) and uploads it to Jira, the read-side twin of the download write fixed earlier.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f4p7-qx46-wc5j", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "b041733473f95119dd539542a43c280737a8e460", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f4p7-qx46-wc5j", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-f4p7-qx46-wc5j", "GHSA-vc25-24vv-fxxm", "GHSA-f6pj-qv47-g96w", "GHSA-mrq8-fv7v-hhjg", "GHSA-wv8v-v4c5-v75j", "GHSA-2xj6-xx86-cwwc", "CVE-2026-77260"], "rd_class": "path-traversal", "attacker": "untrusted-llm-input", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Jira-side sink of the same upload-read family as the confluence row. vc25/f6pj/mrq8/wv8v name both services; 2xj6 reaches the same upload code via update_issue's attachments parameter. Mapping of the multi-service advisories to the Jira sink is by reading the fix diff."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-6vmq-24h2-pj7j", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/sooperset/mcp-atlassian", "sha": "4067d1db4097755cc6add87f95fe3f0746c98c0b", "locator": {"file": "src/mcp_atlassian/jira/attachments.py", "line": 43, "sink_class": "path-traversal", "symbol": "AttachmentsMixin.download_attachment"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "download_attachment's validate_safe_path() defaults base_dir to os.getcwd(), so a target path inside the working directory root (e.g. an importable app module) is accepted; overwriting it gives code execution.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6vmq-24h2-pj7j", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "b041733473f95119dd539542a43c280737a8e460", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6vmq-24h2-pj7j", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-6vmq-24h2-pj7j", "CVE-2026-77271"], "rd_class": "path-traversal", "attacker": "untrusted-llm-input", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Explicit bypass of the 0.17.0 fix for GHSA-xjgw-4wvw-rgm4 (CVE-2026-27825). The same omnibus commit adds the refusal to write into the CWD root."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-3r68-hf9h-887v", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/sooperset/mcp-atlassian", "sha": "4067d1db4097755cc6add87f95fe3f0746c98c0b", "locator": {"file": "src/mcp_atlassian/servers/main.py", "line": 212, "sink_class": "auth-bypass", "symbol": "_list_tools_mcp"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "ENABLED_TOOLS, toolset and read-only filters are applied only in _list_tools_mcp; tools/call dispatches from the full registry, so any client that knows a tool name can call a tool the operator disabled (the fix adds _call_tool_mcp with the same authorization check).", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3r68-hf9h-887v", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "b041733473f95119dd539542a43c280737a8e460", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3r68-hf9h-887v", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-3r68-hf9h-887v", "CVE-2026-77243"], "rd_class": "authz-bypass", "attacker": "remote-authed-user", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "The vulnerable behaviour is an absent call-time check; the locator is the listing-only filter that should also guard dispatch."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-cc5h-2pwp-pvcc", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/sooperset/mcp-atlassian", "sha": "4067d1db4097755cc6add87f95fe3f0746c98c0b", "locator": {"file": "src/mcp_atlassian/servers/main.py", "line": 445, "sink_class": "auth-bypass", "symbol": "UserTokenMiddleware.__call__"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "In the documented multi-user streamable-http deployment the middleware lets requests with no user identity through; the handler then falls back to the operator's global Atlassian credentials, so unauthenticated network clients can invoke every tool.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cc5h-2pwp-pvcc", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "b041733473f95119dd539542a43c280737a8e460", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cc5h-2pwp-pvcc", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-cc5h-2pwp-pvcc", "CVE-2026-77248"], "rd_class": "authz-bypass", "attacker": "remote-unauth", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Fix adds a 401 for identity-less requests unless ALLOW_GLOBAL_CRED_FALLBACK is set. GHSA-wrhw (critical, AtlassianOpaqueTokenVerifier accepts any token) cites the same commit but its diff does not touch the verifier: deferred, see notes."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-6529-c226-h328", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/sooperset/mcp-atlassian", "sha": "4067d1db4097755cc6add87f95fe3f0746c98c0b", "locator": {"file": "src/mcp_atlassian/servers/dependencies.py", "line": 593, "sink_class": "other", "symbol": "_get_fetcher"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The redirect-blocking SSRF hook was attached only in the header-PAT branch of _get_fetcher; the basic-auth and OAuth branches build fetchers without it, so an attacker-controlled Jira/Confluence URL can redirect requests to internal hosts.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6529-c226-h328", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "b041733473f95119dd539542a43c280737a8e460", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6529-c226-h328", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-6529-c226-h328", "CVE-2026-77261"], "rd_class": "ssrf", "attacker": "remote-authed-user", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Incomplete fix of GHSA-7r34-79r5-rcc9 (fix 5cd697d). Fix adds attach_ssrf_hook=True to the basic and OAuth branches and a session-level hook in the client constructors."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-hgcf-4mq8-5266", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/sooperset/mcp-atlassian", "sha": "4067d1db4097755cc6add87f95fe3f0746c98c0b", "locator": {"file": "src/mcp_atlassian/utils/urls.py", "line": 92, "sink_class": "other", "symbol": "validate_url_for_ssrf"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "validate_url_for_ssrf trusts urlparse().hostname, so http://localhost\\@evil.com/ validates as evil.com while requests/WHATWG connect to localhost; the fix rejects a backslash in the authority.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hgcf-4mq8-5266", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "b041733473f95119dd539542a43c280737a8e460", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hgcf-4mq8-5266", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-hgcf-4mq8-5266", "CVE-2026-77274"], "rd_class": "ssrf", "attacker": "remote-authed-user", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Parser differential between the SSRF gate (urlparse) and the executor (requests/urllib3). Bypass of the SSRF guard added for GHSA-7r34-79r5-rcc9."}}
