{"id": "kbc-ghsa-5r34-2g38-6569", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai-agents/praisonaiagents/tools/web_crawl_tools.py", "line": 142, "sink_class": "ssrf-url-fetch", "symbol": "_crawl_with_httpx"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "web_crawl validated only the first URL, then httpx followed redirects automatically, so a public page can 302 the crawler to loopback/metadata addresses.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5r34-2g38-6569", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5r34-2g38-6569", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-5r34-2g38-6569", "GHSA-vg6p-v9vm-6fgj", "GHSA-8hjw-25cg-g52h", "CVE-2026-55525"], "rd_class": "ssrf", "attacker": "untrusted-llm-input", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Three advisories on one sink. Incomplete-fix chain: GHSA-qq9r-63f6-v542 / GHSA-8f4v-xfm9-3244 (1.5.128) added the first-URL check; these bypass it via redirect and unchecked fallback."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-x44h-65qv-cw74", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai-agents/praisonaiagents/tools/spider_tools.py", "line": 61, "sink_class": "ssrf-url-fetch", "symbol": "_host_is_blocked"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The spider tool's host guard only blocked literal IPs (inet_aton); hostnames resolving to private addresses passed, so DNS names reach internal services.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x44h-65qv-cw74", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x44h-65qv-cw74", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-x44h-65qv-cw74", "CVE-2026-55526"], "rd_class": "ssrf", "attacker": "untrusted-llm-input", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "New bypass of prior fix 004dcfef (GHSA-q9pw-vmhh-384g)."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-rg5q-pp8p-f7jm", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai/praisonai/jobs/models.py", "line": 63, "sink_class": "ssrf-url-fetch", "symbol": "JobSubmitRequest.validate_webhook_url"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The jobs webhook URL validator swallows DNS resolution errors (except gaierror: pass), so an unresolvable-at-check, resolvable-at-use hostname (rebinding) bypasses the private-IP rule.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rg5q-pp8p-f7jm", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rg5q-pp8p-f7jm", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-rg5q-pp8p-f7jm", "CVE-2026-55537"], "rd_class": "ssrf", "attacker": "remote-unauth", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Chain: GHSA-8frj-8q3m-xhgm (4.5.128, first webhook SSRF) -> GHSA-rjvw-7vvw-549v (DNS rebinding, 4.6.59) -> this fail-open. The file has the same pattern twice (two models); the first is used."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-ch89-h4r2-c8f8", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai/praisonai/code/utils/file_utils.py", "line": 252, "sink_class": "path-traversal", "symbol": "is_path_within_directory"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The workspace containment check used abspath instead of realpath, so a symlink inside the workspace escapes it for agent read/write tools.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-ch89-h4r2-c8f8", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-ch89-h4r2-c8f8", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-ch89-h4r2-c8f8", "CVE-2026-55540"], "rd_class": "path-traversal", "attacker": "untrusted-llm-input", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Same family as GHSA-gcq3-mfvh-3x25 (code agent tools fail open w/o workspace)."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-hxmv-c4g6-5fqc", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai-agents/praisonaiagents/workflows/workflows.py", "line": 2963, "sink_class": "code-exec", "symbol": "_execute_include"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "A workflow 'include' of a recipe directory exec_module()s that directory's tools.py without the PRAISONAI_ALLOW_LOCAL_TOOLS opt-in that guards the other autoload paths, so a crafted recipe runs arbitrary Python at load.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hxmv-c4g6-5fqc", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hxmv-c4g6-5fqc", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-hxmv-c4g6-5fqc", "CVE-2026-55522"], "rd_class": "code-injection", "attacker": "library-caller", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Incomplete fix of GHSA-xcmw-grxf-wjhj (tool_override autoload gate, 4.6.32): sibling load path."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-6g6r-q6gw-w8fg", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai/praisonai/browser/server.py", "line": 186, "sink_class": "missing-origin-websocket", "symbol": "_handle_connection"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The Browser Server's WebSocket Origin check uses re.match() with an unanchored chrome-extension://[a-z0-9]{32} pattern, so any origin merely starting with that prefix passes and a web page can hijack the browser-automation socket.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6g6r-q6gw-w8fg", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6g6r-q6gw-w8fg", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-6g6r-q6gw-w8fg", "CVE-2026-55536"], "rd_class": "dns-rebinding", "attacker": "malicious-web-content", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Patch bypass of GHSA-8x8f-54wf-vv92 (the advisory that introduced the origin check)."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-pvph-5j39-v8qc", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai/praisonai/mcp_server/transports/http_stream.py", "line": 148, "sink_class": "missing-origin-websocket", "symbol": "HTTPStreamTransport._validate_origin"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The MCP HTTP-stream transport's Origin allowlist uses startswith(), so http://localhost.attacker.com is accepted and a web page can drive the unauthenticated local MCP server.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pvph-5j39-v8qc", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pvph-5j39-v8qc", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-pvph-5j39-v8qc", "CVE-2026-55532"], "rd_class": "dns-rebinding", "attacker": "malicious-web-content", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Same prefix-match bug class as the Browser Server and MCP SSE origin advisories."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-7g3p-92qq-8wvh", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai-agents/praisonaiagents/server/server.py", "line": 139, "sink_class": "auth-bypass", "symbol": "AgentServer._create_app.events"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "AgentServer accepts an auth_token in its config but never checks it: the /events and /publish routes serve any caller, exposing agent activity and letting them publish events.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7g3p-92qq-8wvh", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7g3p-92qq-8wvh", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-7g3p-92qq-8wvh", "CVE-2026-55528"], "rd_class": "authz-bypass", "attacker": "remote-unauth", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Earlier fixes in the same family: GHSA-f292-66h9-fpmf (A2U SSE, 4.5.115)."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-7ww9-85pg-cv4x", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai/praisonai/cli/features/serve.py", "line": 408, "sink_class": "auth-bypass", "symbol": "ServeHandler._create_unified_app"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "`praisonai serve ... --api-key K` stored the key in config but never installed any middleware, so the served agent endpoints stayed unauthenticated even though the operator set a key.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7ww9-85pg-cv4x", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7ww9-85pg-cv4x", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-7ww9-85pg-cv4x", "GHSA-r7v3-x45f-g7hp", "GHSA-pvxx-r596-f5qj", "CVE-2026-55534"], "rd_class": "authz-bypass", "attacker": "remote-unauth", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Three advisories, one missing enforcement. Chain: GHSA-6rmh-7xcm-cpxj (legacy API server auth disabled, 4.6.34) -> these (4.6.58) -> GHSA-892r-p3jq-jp24 (AgentOS still unauthenticated, 4.6.59)."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-2jgc-f764-c5r2", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai/praisonai/jobs/server.py", "line": 127, "sink_class": "auth-bypass", "symbol": "create_app"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The async Jobs API installs its router with no auth middleware or dependency, so any caller who can reach it submits agent jobs, reads results and cancels or deletes jobs.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2jgc-f764-c5r2", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2jgc-f764-c5r2", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-2jgc-f764-c5r2", "CVE-2026-55539"], "rd_class": "authz-bypass", "attacker": "remote-unauth", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Fix adds an opt-in JobsAPIKeyMiddleware (PRAISONAI_JOBS_API_KEY)."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-gfq8-hmph-9gjv", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai/praisonai/recipe/serve.py", "line": 333, "sink_class": "auth-bypass", "symbol": "APIKeyAuthMiddleware.dispatch"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "The Recipe server's api-key/JWT middleware falls open (call_next) when auth is enabled but no key or secret is configured, so a non-localhost bind passes the CLI check yet serves unauthenticated requests.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gfq8-hmph-9gjv", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gfq8-hmph-9gjv", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-gfq8-hmph-9gjv", "CVE-2026-55533"], "rd_class": "authz-bypass", "attacker": "remote-unauth", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Fail-open default; fix returns 503 'misconfigured'."}}
{"id": "kbc-ghsa-gxmw-5f7x-6g22", "kind": "positive", "repo": "https://github.com/MervinPraison/PraisonAI", "sha": "9991e00f5245de182321288918e7ac1add390d0d", "locator": {"file": "src/praisonai-agents/praisonaiagents/memory/file_memory.py", "line": 135, "sink_class": "path-traversal", "symbol": "FileMemory.__init__"}, "expected": {"verdict": "QUALIFIES", "failed_gate": null, "reason_class": "ADVISORY-FIXED", "dedup": null}, "reason": "FileMemory uses user_id as a directory name unsanitised, so '../' sequences write memory files outside the memory root.", "source": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gxmw-5f7x-6g22", "label_origin": "rd-kbc", "kbc": {"fix_sha": "2f9677abb2ea68eab864ee8b6a828fd0141612e1", "advisory_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gxmw-5f7x-6g22", "advisory_ids": ["GHSA-gxmw-5f7x-6g22", "CVE-2026-55527"], "rd_class": "path-traversal", "attacker": "library-caller", "language": "python", "oracle": null, "notes": "Related earlier advisory: GHSA-766v-q9x3-g744 (memory state leakage and path traversal in multi-agent context handoff, 1.5.115)."}}
